Several people in this thread have said this. I disagree. When I
started playing Nethack, I read the Guidebook and picked Archaeologist
because of this: "They start equipped with the tools for a proper
scientific expedition." That sounded nice and academic :) As I played
more, I found the Archaeologist early game to be, in fact, the most
enjoyable for me and my natural playstyle: they start with enough food
to counteract my tendency to dawdle, a sack for my pack-rat impulses,
and of course the incredibly useful tinning kit (poison resistance
ho!). Valkyries, one of the standard noob recommendations, actually
felt more difficult: they kill things easily enough, but I had
constant problems with hunger and inventory management and so on until
I realized they needed a different approach, one which I liked less.

Now I'm still noobish; I haven't made it beyond the castle (my first-
ever castle conquerer, an Archaeologist, choked eating a silver dragon
corpse while satiated, while carrying a charged tinning kit, in
possession of all the corpse-granted intrinsics except disintegration
AND in full knowledge that silver dragon corpses don't confer
intrinsics *headdesk*), but I still prefer to play Archaeologists. The
starting tools rock, the quest is a laugh, dual-wielded silver sabers
are quite nice and Expert divination is faaaaabulous. The crappy
starting armor and weapon are problems that can be solved in due time
by killing monsters and stealing their stuff; normally I try to hang
on with the pickaxe/mattock until I find a silver saber, but in a
pinch orcs have lots of scimitars.

My other favorites are Monk, Tourist and Healer. :)


